# The call names JSON.stringify and leaves the replacer out. It goes to the stub of that built-in, which writes a string, a number, a boolean or null itself, and not to the host function.
# CHECK-LABEL: f1: size=
# CHECK-NOT: CallHostFunction
# CHECK: stub CallBoxedBuiltin.JSONStringify.n2 x1
# CHECK-NOT: CallHostFunction
# A value that is proven a string or a number goes the same way: no string builder is begun for one string or one number.
# CHECK-LABEL: f2: size=
# CHECK-NOT: StringBuilder
